          <div class="partner-body">
            <p class="tag">Water and Plumbing</p>
            <h2>Camco EvoFlex2 25-ft RV Drinking Water Hose</h2>
            <p>A 25-foot hose designed for connecting an RV to a drinking water hookup.</p>

            <aside aria-labelledby="water-hose-take" class="pick-assessment">
              <h3 id="water-hose-take">Jerry&#x2019;s take</h3>
              <p>I understand that nobody needs to be told they need a fresh water hose. However, if you've ever tried
                to roll up and pack a traditional
                fresh water hose in 40-degree weather after a cold front came through overnight you know how stiff those
                traditional hoses can become. Plus
                they take up more valuable space in the storage compartment. This hose is collapsable, and remains
                flexible even in cold weather. I've
                got two of these just in case there's a long run to the shore water hookup. BTW... I couldn't find an
                equivalent 'black tank rinse' hose in
                Amazon's RV supplies section. But they are available as standard collapsable garden hoses in the Home
                and Garden section.
            </aside>

            <a target="_amazon" class="button button-dark" href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09Z6X4RVV">View on
              Amazon</a>
          </div>
        </article>
